      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Focusing on equality of opportunity means ensuring all applicants have a fair chance to be evaluated without discriminatory rules, which maintains predictive integrity. However, some critiques argue that this approach can still allow disparate impact to occur even if the initial rules are unbiased. To fully meet strong ESG mandates, proactively guiding outcomes is often necessary to demonstrate meaningful societal impact rather than just procedural fairness.",
      "source": "target",
